7dpu|a|Pleasing by delicacy or grace; attracting, but not striking or impressing; of a pleasing and attractive form a color; having slight or diminutive beauty; neat or elegant without elevation or grandeur; pleasingly, but not grandly, conceived or expressed; as, a pretty face; a pretty flower; a pretty poem. ; Moderately large; considerable; as, he had saved a pretty fortune. ; Affectedly nice; foppish; -- used in an ill sense. ; Mean; despicable; contemptible; -- used ironically; as, a pretty trick; a pretty fellow. ; Stout; strong and brave; intrepid; valiant. ; In some degree; moderately; considerably; rather; almost; -- less emphatic than very; as, I am pretty sure of the fact; pretty cold weather.	j:3xew,72,6;944m,63,4;8g5f,63,3;45gt,63,3;945h,58,10;71c7,57,204;4zjz,53,10;6632,52,11;8ant,52,2;8bat,52,3;6k0h,51,6;7e8k,50,22;9ayp,50,5;50i0,49,16;2kur,49,4~90mt,16,4638;945e,40,2276;a6i1,39,2022;685d,47,1564;2eh,27,1422;1up2,27,1224;36dg,3,685;a62g,16,639;ai6u,10,631;5r2n,33,617;74mm,18,583;78ce,36,523;8ewu,8,516;6js4,34,497;6kh7,1,480	e:a4ll,54,11;6cr,28,6;965k,22,3;5ni,11,88;3qu,7,6099;9yq7,7,178;348,5,2;3uo,4,4;3lw7,2,927;a7kn,1,1582;1gf5,1,6~3qu,7,6099;a7kn,1,1582;3lw7,2,927;9yq7,7,178;5ni,11,88;a4ll,54,11;6cr,28,6;1gf5,1,6;3uo,4,4;965k,22,3;348,5,2
