7hcp|n|The relation or adaptation of one portion to another, or to the whole, as respect magnitude, quantity, or degree; comparative relation; ratio; as, the proportion of the parts of a building, or of the body. ; Harmonic relation between parts, or between different things of the same kind; symmetrical arrangement or adjustment; symmetry; as, to be out of proportion. ; The portion one receives when a whole is distributed by a rule or principle; equal or proper share; lot. ; A part considered comparatively; a share. ; The equality or similarity of ratios, especially of geometrical ratios; or a relation among quantities such that the quotient of the first divided by the second is equal to that of the third divided by the fourth; -- called also geometrical proportion, in distinction from arithmetical proportion, or that in which the difference of the first and second is equal to the difference of the third and fourth. ; The rule of three, in arithmetic, in which the three given terms, together with the one sought, are proportional.	a:8qdj,87,36;6s7b,86,5;3srt,85,7;8qdc,84,46;lup,75,5;97p2,72,4;9uvz,71,3;97py,67,155;5ugn,65,11;6s7a,65,3;8ogv,63,689;93h6,61,4;xsx,59,158;20un,59,70;h7a,56,8~53yv,54,1571;8s1h,45,1066;88v3,18,968;8ogv,63,689;43ai,44,685;43bd,48,612;2gos,45,370;8906,38,353;53zu,44,340;3uh4,47,320;7aas,36,311;4lx1,52,306;8s28,38,211;9vgb,8,189;3sqe,4,184	v:90gj,58,4;48ta,53,3;308o,44,34;2g9m,38,3;59fn,36,33;3voq,27,16;4f2a,25,48;6ju8,23,18;33h0,20,97;1tqk,19,9;a9md,18,9;1vsq,14,38;4f20,11,8;5vos,11,6;6t9e,10,1~33h0,20,97;4f2a,25,48;1vsq,14,38;308o,44,34;59fn,36,33;6ju8,23,18;3voq,27,16;17wl,10,11;a9md,18,9;5i41,4,9;1tqk,19,9;4f20,11,8;5vos,11,6;90gj,58,4;48ta,53,3	V:a81r,52,3;9hlv,40,4;9agv,33,4;a9fk,26,15;1phr,16,30;9hmj,15,11;33qn,5,13~1phr,16,30;a9fk,26,15;33qn,5,13;9hmj,15,11;9hlv,40,4;9agv,33,4;a81r,52,3	n:48mt,79,3;97p2,68,3;79qw,67,361;7drc,46,4;1sr2,24,3;2g7q,18,1;2ji5,17,5;8906,5,35~79qw,67,361;8906,5,35;2ji5,17,5;7drc,46,4;97p2,68,3;1sr2,24,3;48mt